 "final_message": "All twelve items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n  - **Parsing:** blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines are skipped but still counted in the `line N` numbers.\n  - **`converted` values:** `1`, `0` and empty become `True`, `False` and `None`.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added `test_conversion_rate_none_counts_as_not_converted` and `test_dedupe_sessions_keeps_last_duplicate` to `tests/test_metrics.py`.\n- **Item 11:** In `README.md`, the `conversions_in_window` entry now says the last `days` entries, and there is a new `daily_conversion_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest of the package turned up three more deviations, all fixed:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name. It returns nothing when `n` is 0 or negative, which the spec doesn't say.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts its keys.\n  - `longest_conversion_streak` never reset its run count after a zero day, so it now does.\n\nSPEC section 4 doesn't say what to do with a `converted` field that isn't `1`, `0` or empty. I made that raise `ValueError` with the `line N` message, like the other malformed-line cases. Tell me if you'd rather it be handled differently.",
